check_failing.description:
The HA Watcher entry **{watcher}** reports that the check **{check}** is failing:

> {message}

This item clears by itself when the watcher reports the check as ok again. Use **Ignore** to hide it meanwhile; it stays hidden while the check keeps failing.

check_failing_entity.description:
The HA Watcher entry **{watcher}** reports that the check **{check}** is failing:

> {message}

Home Assistant can try to fix this by reloading the integration that provides `{entity}`. This item clears by itself when the watcher reports the check as ok again. Use **Ignore** to hide it meanwhile; it stays hidden while the check keeps failing.

check_failing_backup.description:
The HA Watcher entry **{watcher}** reports that the check **{check}** is failing:

> {message}

Home Assistant can try to fix this by starting a backup now. This item clears by itself when the watcher reports the check as ok again. Use **Ignore** to hide it meanwhile; it stays hidden while the check keeps failing.
